# Muffin Trash

## Plugin semantics

`muffin/trash` adds soft-delete via `Muffin/Trash.Trash` behavior: `delete()` marks `deleted`/`trashed` (or configured field) instead of removing the row; finds exclude trashed rows by default.

## Required behavior

- Apply only when `muffin/trash` ^4 is installed.
- Add the behavior on Tables that own soft-delete; ensure the datetime column exists.
- Prefer Trash APIs (`trash`, `restoreTrash`, `emptyTrash`, `purge` option) over hand-rolled `deleted_at` filters.
- Hard delete only intentionally (`purge` / `emptyTrash`) with authorization.
- Do not invent Laravel SoftDeletes traits as the CakePHP default.

## Anti-patterns

- Parallel manual `WHERE deleted IS NULL` when Trash already scopes finds
- Hard-deleting by accident in apps that standardize on Trash
- Assuming Trash when the package is absent
